00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Hi everyone! In this chapter, we will be solving some questions and we will solve them using a special type of algorithm which is called Divide and Conquer.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
So in this chapter, we will solve all the questions with the help of the Divide and Conquer strategy.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
First of all, let's talk about the Divide and Conquer strategy.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
If I talk about Divide, then Divide means that it happens in English to break something or divide something.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
So what we will do is, whatever big problem we have, sometimes it happens that in coding and in life, big problems get very big and it becomes very difficult to solve them.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000
So what we will do is, we divide our problems into small parts, small parts and small parts.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:49,000
So what I will do is, I will divide my big problem into small parts and then I will solve these small problems first.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Because it is easier to solve a small problem than a big problem.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
So as soon as I solve these small problems, more than half of my work will be completed.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
So this will be the strategy whenever we will talk about Divide.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
After that, the second step is always Conquer. Conquer means that it happens in English to break something.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:16,000
So as soon as I have taken out the solution of these small problems, what I will do is, I will connect those solutions and take out the solution of my big problem.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:26,000
So what I did is, I divided my big problem into small parts and then I converted their small solution into a big solution.

14
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
So in this way, I took out a big solution of a big problem in a different way.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
If you are interested in the history and social sciences, then we had read a strategy about the Britishers.

16
