What the Britishers used to do in the beginning of India was, they used something called Divide and Rule Strategy.

17
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
What the Britishers used to do was, they used the strategy of the King or the rest of the Indians.

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:58,000
They first divided us here and there, then put the foot and then put the rule strategy.

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
So putting the foot was basically dividing and after that, rule and rule, when people start fighting themselves.

20
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
After that, it will be easier to rule on them.

21
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
So there, they used Divide and Conquer in an evil way.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Here we are not using it to do any bad things or we are using it to solve problems.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
It is a very same strategy.

24
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:26,000
There is a problem in front of you, you have to divide it into small parts and it is very easy to get the solution out of small parts.

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:34,000
So we will take out their solution and when we combine their solutions, we will see that our big problem is automatically solved.

26
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
So now let's solve some problems in our Divide and Conquer chapter.

